  "decision_conditions": [
    "The siting, scale, and design of the rear extension would be a contrived and cramped form of development that presents as an insensitive addition to the host property and overdevelopment of the site, contrary to Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012, and Council's Residential Design Supplementary Planning Guidance 2013.",
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate through the submission of cogent information that the proposed extension would not have an unacceptable adverse impact on the closest principal habitable room windows at No. 67 Ancaster Crescent and 99 Bargate Close in terms of daylight/sunlight. Given the scale of the extension and the proximity of neighbouring windows it is considered that there is a likelihood that the development would breach the \"BRE 45 Degree Rule\" and reduce light entering into the neighbouring habitable room, which in turn would harm the residential amenities of the occupants of the neighbouring property. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
